{"instance_id": "pallets__flask-6071", "repo": "pallets/flask", "base_commit": "8285adf5a4f572dbf7a0a3b8f3a96ca0b19c50a4", "issue_url": "https://github.com/pallets/flask/issues/6071", "query": "Tests fail with pytest 9.1: _pytest.monkeypatch.notset removed\nFlask's test suite imports the private notset sentinel from _pytest.monkeypatch in both tests/conftest.py and tests/test_cli.py. pytest 9.1 removed this attribute, moving it to _pytest.compat.NOTSET. This causes a collection-time crash — no tests can run at all.\n\n### Reproducing\n```\npip install -e . pytest==9.1.1\npytest tests/\ntests/test_cli.py:14: in <module>\n    from _pytest.monkeypatch import notset\nE   ImportError: cannot import name 'notset' from '_pytest.monkeypatch'\n```\nEven after fixing test_cli.py, every test fails because tests/conftest.py accesses monkeypatch.notset as a module attribute in the _standard_os_environ session fixture:\n\n`tests/conftest.py:19: AttributeError: module '_pytest.monkeypatch' has no attribute 'notset'`\n### Expected Behavior\nThe test suite should work with pytest 9.1+.\n\n### Environment:\n\nPython version: 3.15.0b2\nFlask version: 3.1.3", "pr_urls": ["https://github.com/pallets/flask/pull/6095"], "weak_targets": ["tests/conftest.py/_reset_os_environ", "tests/conftest.py/_standard_os_environ", "tests/test_cli.py/test_disable_dotenv_from_env", "tests/test_cli.py/test_dotenv_optional", "tests/test_cli.py/test_dotenv_path", "tests/test_cli.py/test_load_dotenv"], "weak_source_targets": [], "modified_test_functions": ["tests/conftest.py/_reset_os_environ", "tests/conftest.py/_standard_os_environ", "tests/test_cli.py/test_disable_dotenv_from_env", "tests/test_cli.py/test_dotenv_optional", "tests/test_cli.py/test_dotenv_path", "tests/test_cli.py/test_load_dotenv"], "review_flags": ["multi_function_pr"], "candidate_evaluations": [{"positive_id": "tests/conftest.py/_reset_os_environ", "semantic_similarity": 0.385506, "semantic_status": "computed", "llm_relevance_label": "necessary_helper", "llm_judge_status": "completed_unverified", "llm_evidence": "Removing this private-state reset supports replacing the session fixture with per-test environment cleanup."}, {"positive_id": "tests/conftest.py/_standard_os_environ", "semantic_similarity": 0.475783, "semantic_status": "computed", "llm_relevance_label": "fix_target", "llm_judge_status": "completed_unverified", "llm_evidence": "Fixture directly accesses removed monkeypatch.notset, causing the reported setup failure."}, {"positive_id": "tests/test_cli.py/test_disable_dotenv_from_env", "semantic_similarity": 0.368987, "semantic_status": "computed", "llm_relevance_label": "uncertain", "llm_judge_status": "completed_unverified", "llm_evidence": "No supplied diff changes this test; its code does not reference removed APIs."}, {"positive_id": "tests/test_cli.py/test_dotenv_optional", "semantic_similarity": 0.31431, "semantic_status": "computed", "llm_relevance_label": "test_change", "llm_judge_status": "completed_unverified", "llm_evidence": "Adds explicit FOO cleanup to improve test isolation."}, {"positive_id": "tests/test_cli.py/test_dotenv_path", "semantic_similarity": 0.364896, "semantic_status": "computed", "llm_relevance_label": "test_change", "llm_judge_status": "completed_unverified", "llm_evidence": "Test uses removed notset sentinel, but its specific modification is absent from supplied diffs."}, {"positive_id": "tests/test_cli.py/test_load_dotenv", "semantic_similarity": 0.348919, "semantic_status": "computed", "llm_relevance_label": "test_change", "llm_judge_status": "completed_unverified", "llm_evidence": "Replaces private sentinel bookkeeping with public monkeypatch.delenv calls in test setup."}], "groundtruth_status": "unverified_multi_target_candidates"}
{"instance_id": "pallets__flask-6093", "repo": "pallets/flask", "base_commit": "514fc6b3e8402e4c646d5284e97a4f0ab50a7c4b", "issue_url": "https://github.com/pallets/flask/issues/6093", "query": "IPv6 addresses parsed incorrectly because of `.partition(\":\")`?\nHi, I checked the code and saw that two places use `.partition(\":\")` on addresses, and IPv6 addresses contain \":\".\n\nThis breaks 1. `session_transaction` value setting, and 2. `Flask.run()` if `SERVER_NAME` is set. I've already prepared two tests that fail, you can use them to reproduce:\n\n1. In `test_testing.py`\n```\ndef test_session_transaction_ipv6(app):\n    base_url = \"http://[::1]:8000/\"\n    client = app.test_client()\n\n    @app.get(\"/\")\n    def index():\n        return str(flask.session.get(\"value\"))\n\n    with client.session_transaction(base_url=base_url) as sess:\n        sess[\"value\"] = 42\n\n    assert client.get(\"/\", base_url=base_url).text == \"42\"\n```\n\n2. Add one case to `test_run_from_config`\n```\n(None, None, \"[::1]:8080\", \"::1\", 8080),\n```\n\nIs this known and intended? I could send the patches for these two places.", "pr_urls": ["https://github.com/pallets/flask/pull/6096"], "weak_targets": ["src/flask/app.py/Flask/run", "src/flask/testing.py/FlaskClient/session_transaction"], "weak_source_targets": ["src/flask/app.py/Flask/run", "src/flask/testing.py/FlaskClient/session_transaction"], "modified_test_functions": [], "review_flags": ["multi_function_pr"], "candidate_evaluations": [{"positive_id": "src/flask/app.py/Flask/run", "semantic_similarity": 0.332614, "semantic_status": "computed", "llm_relevance_label": "fix_target", "llm_judge_status": "cache_hit_unverified", "llm_evidence": "Replaces SERVER_NAME colon partitioning with URL parsing to correctly extract IPv6 host and port."}, {"positive_id": "src/flask/testing.py/FlaskClient/session_transaction", "semantic_similarity": 0.318889, "semantic_status": "computed", "llm_relevance_label": "fix_target", "llm_judge_status": "cache_hit_unverified", "llm_evidence": "Replaces request host colon partitioning with URL parsing for IPv6 session cookie handling."}], "groundtruth_status": "unverified_multi_target_candidates"}
